# Template for the DEBIAN/control file inside the staged package root.
# packaging/deb/build-deb.sh fills in @VERSION@ and writes the result; this
# file is not itself valid control syntax and is not installed anywhere.
#
# One stanza, not a source-package Source:/Build-Depends: pair, because this
# is built by dpkg-deb directly rather than by dpkg-buildpackage -- see
# build-deb.sh's own header for why cargo-deb and debhelper both assume a
# single [package] Cargo manifest that this virtual workspace does not have.
Package: cordial
Version: @VERSION@
Section: games
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: luohoa97 <luohoa97@users.noreply.github.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/luohoa97/cordial
# Hand-translated from the same soname list packaging/rpm/cordial.spec's
# Requires: and packaging/aur/cordial-git/PKGBUILD's depends() already carry,
# into Debian/Ubuntu package names rather than generated by dpkg-shlibdeps.
# dpkg-shlibdeps reads the built binary's own DT_NEEDED entries and would be
# the more exact source of truth, but it wants the full debhelper substvars
# machinery (${shlibs:Depends}) around it; this list is the same one three
# other packaging formats already carry, kept in step by hand for the same
# reason those already are. Run `lintian` and `dpkg-shlibdeps -O` against a
# built .deb before trusting this list unchanged across a dependency bump.
#
# libpipewire0.3-0 is not listed: native/pipewire_backend.cpp dlopen's it
# rather than linking it, so its absence is a loss of audio rather than a
# missing-library failure at install time -- the same reasoning
# packaging/rpm/cordial.spec gives for listing it as a soname Requires
# anyway. Debian's dependency resolution has no dlopen-aware equivalent to
# rpm's soname Requires, so it is listed here too, as an ordinary Depends,
# rather than left implicit.
Depends: libgtk-4-1, libadwaita-1-0, libwebkitgtk-6.0-4,
 libglib2.0-0, libpango-1.0-0, libgraphene-1.0-0, libsoup-3.0-0,
 libgcc-s1, libstdc++6, libc6, libvulkan1, libwayland-client0,
 libwayland-egl1, libxkbcommon0, libegl1, libgles2, libpipewire-0.3-0,
 hicolor-icon-theme
# **No `deno` dependency, and that is not an oversight.** Plugins are Deno
# programs (ADR-008) and Cordial bundles no runtime, so without `deno` on PATH
# every plugin fails to spawn. There is no `deno` package to require:
# `dnf5 list deno` on Fedora 44 returns nothing, and Debian ships none either,
# so naming one would make this package uninstallable -- strictly worse than
# the bug. The client says so itself when a plugin cannot start, and the README
# tells users to install it. Bundling the runtime is the real fix and is not
# done yet; see docs/NEXT.md.
Recommends: sober
Description: run Roblox's official Android build natively on Linux
 Cordial loads Roblox's official Android x86-64 libroblox.so natively: a
 ported AOSP bionic linker, a bionic/glibc shim, libjnivm in place of
 Android's ART, and a framework layer that answers the calls the client
 makes into the platform. There is no emulator, no container and no virtual
 machine.
 .
 CORDIAL SHIPS NO ROBLOX BUILD. On first run it offers to fetch one and
 installs it only if Roblox's own signing certificate signed it. Roblox
 publishes no Android binary of its own, so the build comes from a
 third-party mirror, from a copy Sober has already unpacked, or from an APK
 you supply yourself. Run it by typing `cordial`.
 .
 Cordial is early. You can sign in, load an experience and play it with a
 keyboard and mouse, type into text fields and hear sound. Voice chat does
 not work, and on roughly one launch in three a signed-in client reaches the
 home screen and freezes; reopening usually works. See the README for what was
 measured and how: https://github.com/luohoa97/cordial#readme
